    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Pandas live in China. They live in the mountains, where it is cold and wet. There are about 1,800 pandas in the wild today. Many people love pandas, and they are a famous symbol of China."
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "A panda is big. It is about 1.5 metres long and can weigh 100 kilograms. Pandas are black and white. They have black ears, black eyes and black legs."
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Pandas eat a lot of bamboo. A panda eats for twelve hours every day. It eats up to twelve kilograms of bamboo, and it also drinks a lot of water. Pandas sometimes eat small animals or eggs, but not often."
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Baby pandas are very small. A new baby is only about the size of a mouse, and it is pink. It stays with its mother for about two years. Pandas do not live in groups. They live alone, and they sleep about ten hours a day."
      }
    ]
  },
